You need ClearVisn V3.1 (the "web server" version) to manage the CC / CG 
devices (100Mbps and 1Gbps ethernet switches), plus later firmware in the 
DEChub (V5.5 was OK I think, V5.6-1 is the latest I know of) and I'd suggest 
the latest firmware in the VNswitch itself (V3.4.0 I think). I'd avoid CV 
3.0 and I think there were some patches to V3.1 as well.

Another way would be to use the chassis to redirect to the relevant slot, 
then goto the local console, then configure the module at the command line 
interface. That won't let you set up the 100Mbps backplane connectivity 
though - you need ClearVisn V3.1 for that.

