Sounds to me as if it's an as yet unconfigured device, so it's probably 
stuck in the "easystart" loop, which causes it to appear / disappear as far 
as the DEChub 900 is concerned. You need to get to the console to kill that 
by typing "stop" (check with the manuals) while it's sending out messages, 
then configure the DRS at the console interface ("talk 6" then "qconfig" I 
think). The best way I know to get to the console if it's doing this is by 
putting the switch into a DEChub One, then you're not reliant on the 
redirect in the DEChub 900. There might be other ways too, but it's been a 
while since I poked about with this stuff.

